<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David VI Narin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1225–1293</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> VI Narin was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, crowned as co-ruler with his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-vii-ulu">David VII Ulu</a> under Mongol overlordship. In 1259 he rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and, after the rising failed, withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a>, where he ruled western Georgia as a separate kingdom, the origin of the Kingdom of Imereti. He reigned there until his death in 1293.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-vi-narin.jpg" alt="David VI Narin" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:David_Narin,_Gelati_Monastery,_south-east_chapel,_west_wall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
